Body:
Got more argument for this fix to be merged

1) current behavior is ~different~ from env handling. For some unapparent reasons, we allow env vars to be unset, but don't allow files. This is counter intuitive and requires distinct explanation like this: "NOTE: while config allows env vars to be unset, missing files will cause opencode to fail on start". Why having this special ceremony for files when we can make behavior uniform?

2) current behavior breaks opencode UI's worktrees/workspaces

Consider project that has this opencode.json
```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "mcp": {
    "test-secret-server": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": ["sh", "-c", "echo $TEST_API_KEY > /dev/null"],
      "environment": {
        "TEST_API_KEY": "{file:.test-secret}"
      },
      "enabled": true
    }
  }
}
```

It requires `test-secret` to be present in each worktree. If it is not, worktree will  be created but UI will fail to open it, and for each broken worktree it will show multiple notifications, even if currently a healthy worktree is focused

Making missing files to produce "" will fix this behavior. No file, worktree just loads with config and than can be fixed the same way we fix missing env vars

